        "iv_field": "atm_iv",
        "straddle_field": "straddle_ratio",
        "spot_field": "spot",
        "status_field": "status",
        "status_ok": "ok",
        "front_target": 30,
        "back_target": 90,
        "window": 60,
        "min_history": 20,
        "crush_min": 0.12,
        "crush_z_min": 3.0,
        "spread_drop_min": 0.01,
        "refractory": 50,
        "max_market_share": 0.4,
        "min_symbols_for_guard": 10,
        "max_gap_days": 5,
        "entry_lead": 3,
        "exit_lag": 1,
        "scale_floor": 0.01,
        "end_before": "2021-01-01"
      },
      "notes": "The frozen event rules of run-theta-chain-events.json (ADR-0265 Amendment 4), chosen on AAPL 2016-2019 announcements, applied unchanged to the whole universe: a front-30 ATM vol crush of >= 12 log points that is 3 robust sigmas below the name's own trailing 60 sessions, with the 30-90 spread collapsing, no more than 40% of the symbols of a date, at most one event per 50 sessions. The realized move is an OUTPUT, not a criterion. THIS IS A RETROSPECTIVE LABELLER, NOT A LIVE SIGNAL: the entry (event - 3 sessions) precedes the detection date. The detected subset is selected on the vol outcome (EXPLORATORY per Amendment 4)."
